ext Only</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;\n                    <a href=\"javascript:window.print()\">Print</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<a href=\"product_types.php?site=HGX\">Product List</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;\n                    <a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=1&glossary=1\">Glossary On</a></div>\n                <div>Versions:\n                            <b>1</b> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=2&glossary=0\">2</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=3&glossary=0\">3</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=4&glossary=0\">4</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=5&glossary=0\">5</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=6&glossary=0\">6</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=7&glossary=0\">7</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=8&glossary=0\">8</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=9&glossary=0\">9</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=10&glossary=0\">10</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=11&glossary=0\">11</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=12&glossary=0\">12</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=13&glossary=0\">13</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=14&glossary=0\">14</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=15&glossary=0\">15</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=16&glossary=0\">16</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=17&glossary=0\">17</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=18&glossary=0\">18</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=19&glossary=0\">19</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=20&glossary=0\">20</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=21&glossary=0\">21</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=22&glossary=0\">22</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=23&glossary=0\">23</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=24&glossary=0\">24</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=25&glossary=0\">25</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=26&glossary=0\">26</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=27&glossary=0\">27</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=28&glossary=0\">28</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=HGX&issuedby=HGX&product=AFD&format=CI&version=29&glossary=0\">29</a> \n                    <hr size=\"1\" width=\"520\" noshade=\"noshade\" align=\"left\" />\n        </div>\n        <pre class=\"glossaryProduct\">\n706\nFXUS64 KHGX 041751\nAFDHGX\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Houston/Galveston TX\n1251 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\n...New DISCUSSION, AVIATION, MARINE...\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n- Seasonably hot with highs in the 90s and heat index values\n  100-107F each day.\n\n- An isolated late day shower can`t be ruled out along the\n  seabreeze later today and Wednesday, but most locations will\n  remain dry.\n\n- Slightly better rain chances expected Thursday into early next\n  week for southern parts of the region as some deeper moisture\n  flows back inland.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\nIssued at 1251 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nNo significant changes were made to the ongoing forecast. With\nthe exception of an isolated seabreeze/baybreeze shower or\nthunderstorm, subsidence and modest moisture levels should keep\nrain chances fairly low for the vast majority of the region. As\nthe days progress Thursday into early next week, we should see\nheights fall just a touch across our coastal areas as the western\nridge repositions just a bit further north. This, along with a\ndeveloping fetch of SE llvl winds and higher PW`s should allow for\nsome better rain chances (mainly just scattered diurnally driven\ncoverage) for our southern 2-3 tiers of counties. High temperatures\nshould trend down a few degrees as well with the SE flow and more\ncloud cover. 47\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...\n(18Z TAF Issuance)\nIssued at 1251 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nMainly clear skies prevail keeping conditions VFR for the afternoon\nand evening hours. A PROB30 for SH remains over IAH, HOU, and SGR\nbetween 21z today and 01z tomorrow, there is still a less than\n10% chance of TS. Winds will begin to relax to LGT and VRB around\n5-7z across the terminals. This signals for the potential of\nanother round of patchy mist/fog west of I-45 bringing MVFR\nVIS/CIG. CIG/VIS return to VFR after 1500z aided by the increasing\nSSE winds. Wednesday afternoon conditions remain similar to today\nbringing the possible for afternoon SH/TS. CW\n\n&&\n\n.MARINE...\nIssued at 1251 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nTypical summertime pattern will prevail with onshore winds peaking\nin the 10-15kt range and seas generally 2-4ft. Rain chances will\nslightly increase Thursday into early next week...mainly isolated\nto scattered activity in the late night through early afternoon\nhours for the coastal waters. 47\n\n&&\n\n.PRELIMINARY POINT TEMPS/POPS...\nCollege Station (CLL)  77  98  77  97 /   0   0   0   0\nHouston (IAH)  79  98  79  97 /  20  10   0  10\nGalveston (GLS)  83  90  83  90 /  10   0   0  10\n\n&&\n\n.HGX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...\nTX...None.\nGM...None.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...47\nAVIATION...CMW\nMARINE...47\n\n\n</pre>\n\n                </div>\n            <footer>\n                                <div class=\"footer-legal\">\n    <div id=\"footerLogo\" class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-2 col-md-2\">\n        <a href=\"//www.usa.gov\"><img src=\"/css/images/usa_gov.png\" alt=\"usa.gov\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" /></a>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-4 col-md-4\">\n        <ul class=\"list-unstyled footer-legal-content\">\n            <li><a href=\"//www.commerce.gov\">US Dept of Commerce</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"//www.noaa.gov\">National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov\">National Weather Service</a></li>\n                        <li>1325 East West Highway<br /></li>\n                        <li>Silver Spring, MD 20910</li>\n            <li><br /><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov/Contact\">Comments? Questions? Please Contact Us.</a></li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-3 col-md-3\">\n        <ul class=\"list-unstyled\">\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov/disclaimer\">Disclaimer</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"//www.cio.noaa.gov/services_programs/info_quality.html\">Information Quality</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov/help\">Help</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"//www.weather.gov/glossary\">Glossary</a></li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-3 col-md-3\">\n        <ul class=\"list-unstyled\">\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.noaa.gov/foia-freedom-of-information-act\">Freedom of Information Act (FOIA)</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov/about\">About Us</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov/careers\">Career Opportunities</a></li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n            </footer>\n        </main>\n    </body>\n</html>\n",
