    "last_text": "\u0001\n382 \nFXUS64 KLCH 041724\nAFDLCH\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Lake Charles LA\n1224 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\n...New DISCUSSION, AVIATION, MARINE, FIRE WEATHER...\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n- A typical summer weather pattern will prevail through this week \nwith a few afternoon thunderstorms each day. \n\n- Afternoon highs will climb into the low to mid 90s each day \n  with maximum heat indices ranging from 101 to 109.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\n(This evening through next Monday)\nIssued at 1213 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nThe dog days of summer are upon us and the weather \npattern seems to have gotten the message as a persistent and \nsomewhat stagnant weather pattern is expected to continue through \nthe week. The area will remain sandwiched between a sprawling upper \nlevel ridge that continues to bake the southwestern U.S. and an \nupper level low centered over the southeastern U.S. The resulting \nweak gradient aloft will allow for daily, diurnally driven afternoon \nthunderstorms (20-40% chance). Any storms that develop will likely \nhave little forward motion and will, instead, be propagated by \noutflow boundaries and the daily sea breeze. At the surface, weak \nhigh pressure over the central and eastern gulf will maintain light \nsoutherly winds through the weekend. Temperatures will remain near \nseasonal normals with afternoon highs climbing into the low to mid \n90s each day with maximum heat indices ranging from 101-109. \n\nJones\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...\n(18Z TAFS)\nIssued at 1213 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nVFR conditions will prevail through the taf period. A few showers\nand thunderstorms will develop through the afternoon (20-40%)\nalong the inland advancing sea breeze. These will have little \nforward motion and will dissipate by 01Z. Weak high pressure over\nthe northeastern gulf will maintain light southerly winds through\nthe taf period.\n\nJones\n\n&&\n\n.MARINE...\nIssued at 1213 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nLight south to southwest flow will prevail through the \nweekend along with seas of 1-3 feet. Precipitation chances will \nrange from 10-20% each afternoon.\n\n&&\n\n.FIRE WEATHER...\nIssued at 1213 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nKBDI values continue to climb, sitting between 500 to 600. The \nsomewhat lower dewpoints and humidity have departed with minimum \nRH values expected to range from 50% to 60% each afternoon through\nthe rest of the week. Scattered daily afternoon thunderstorms \n(20-40%) are expected each day through the weekend.\n\n&&\n\n.LCH WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...\nLA...None.\nTX...None.\nGM...None.\n&&\n\n$$\n\nPUBLIC/FIRE/MARINE...66\nAVIATION...66\n\n\u0003\n",
